   {
    "question": "$[AB]$ is a chord of a circle with centre $O$ and radius $10$ cm.\n$|AB| = 16$ cm.\nFind the distance from $O$ to the chord $AB$.",
    "level": "ordinary",
    "marks": 10,
    "workedSolution": {
     "steps": [
      {
       "title": "Bisect the chord (Theorem 21)",
       "lines": [
        {
         "text": "The perpendicular from the centre $O$ to the chord meets it at its midpoint $M$ (Theorem 21)."
        },
        {
         "tex": "|AM| &= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 16",
         "sym": "Rational(1,2)*16",
         "new": true
        },
        {
         "tex": "&= 8",
         "sym": "8"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Use Pythagoras in triangle $OMA$",
       "lines": [
        {
         "text": "$OMA$ has a right angle at $M$ and hypotenuse $|OA| = 10$."
        },
        {
         "tex": "|OM|^2 &= 10^2 - 8^2",
         "sym": "Eq(OM**2, 10**2 - 8**2)",
         "new": true
        },
        {
         "tex": "&= 100 - 64",
         "sym": "Eq(OM**2, 100 - 64)"
        },
        {
         "tex": "&= 36",
         "sym": "Eq(OM**2, 36)"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Take the square root",
       "lines": [
        {
         "tex": "|OM| &= 6",
         "sym": "Eq(OM, 6)",
         "new": true
        }
       ]
      }
     ],
     "finalAnswer": "|OM| = 6 \\text{ cm}"
    },
    "finalSym": "6",
    "answerSym": "sqrt(10**2 - (16/2)**2)"
   },
   {
    "question": "A circle has centre $O$ and radius $13$ cm.\n$M$ is the foot of the perpendicular from $O$ to a chord $[PQ]$, and $|OM| = 5$ cm.\nFind $|PQ|$.",
