   {
    "question": "A horizontal pipe has a circular cross-section.\nThe surface of the water in the pipe is a chord of the circle of length $48$ cm.\nThe water is $8$ cm deep at its deepest point, which is directly below the midpoint of the chord.\nFind the radius of the pipe.",
    "level": "ordinary",
    "marks": 15,
    "workedSolution": {
     "steps": [
      {
       "title": "Set up the right-angled triangle",
       "lines": [
        {
         "text": "Let $O$ be the centre and $r$ the radius. The line from $O$ to the midpoint $M$ of the chord is perpendicular to the chord (Theorem 21), so it is the vertical line through the deepest point."
        },
        {
         "text": "Half the chord is $24$ cm, and $|OM| = r - 8$."
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Use Pythagoras in the triangle with sides $r$, $24$ and $r-8$",
       "lines": [
        {
         "tex": "r^2 &= 24^2 + (r-8)^2",
         "sym": "Eq(r**2, 24**2 + (r-8)**2)",
         "new": true
        },
        {
         "tex": "&= 576 + r^2 - 16r + 64",
         "sym": "Eq(r**2, 576 + r**2 - 16*r + 64)"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Solve for $r$",
       "lines": [
        {
         "tex": "16r &= 640",
         "sym": "Eq(16*r, 640)"
        },
        {
         "tex": "r &= 40",
         "sym": "Eq(r, 40)"
        }
       ]
      }
     ],
     "finalAnswer": "r = 40 \\text{ cm}"
    },
    "finalSym": "40",
    "answerSym": "(24**2 + 8**2)/(2*8)"
   }
  ]
 },
